# Files that are exempt from the test-coverage check.
# One path per line, relative to the binate repo root.
# Example: pkg/builtins/rt/rt.bn

# pkg/bootstrap/bootstrap.bn: format helpers for the print/println
# builtin (formatInt, formatBool). The test-runner infrastructure
# can't currently run unit tests in pkg/bootstrap as a regular
# Binate package — the synthetic test runner has shape issues with
# the @[]char return type (`return ""` reads back as len > 0).
# Likely needs a forked test runner for bootstrap, in line with
# the future conformance-test fork the user has in mind. The
# helpers themselves are exercised end-to-end by the conformance
# suite's println tests across all modes.
pkg/bootstrap/bootstrap.bn

# === TEMPORARY (grandfathered 2026-06-20) ===========================
# impls/ stdlib/runtime files that don't yet meet the per-file _test.bn
# bar (the check was extended to impls/ on 2026-06-20).  The standard is
# per-file tests with very few genuine exceptions; these are grandfathered
# pending the test-reorganization follow-up (claude-todo.md, "Reorganize
# stdlib tests to meet per-file test-coverage"):
#   * math per-function files SHOULD get their own _test.bn (atanh_test.bn …);
#   * os per-platform files SHOULD be amalgamated via #[build] then tested;
#   * the strconv atof_* splits are exercised by atof_test.bn;
#   * the baremetal bootstrap/rt variants share the bootstrap exception above.
# Whittle this list toward "very few" as the follow-up lands.
impls/core/baremetal/pkg/bootstrap/bootstrap.bn
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/rt/rt_baremetal.bn
